1
00:02:00,170 --> 00:02:02,838
<v Man> Oh, hi Ruth. How are you?

2
00:02:02,838 --> 00:02:06,834
<v Woman> I’m sorry to bother you, Alastair, but I’ve been having some problems.

3
00:02:06,834 --> 00:02:10,436
<v Man> Oh. Come on in ... What’s happened?

4
00:02:10,436 --> 00:02:27,592
<v Woman> Basically, I had a leak from one of the pipes in the bathroom and water started coming through downstairs and the kitchen ceiling’s badly stained. I’ve got the leak fixed temporarily but I wasn’t happy with the plumber and I wanted to ask your advice.

5
00:02:27,592 --> 00:02:37,997
<v Man> Of course ... Well, the first thing I’d say is make sure you choose a local company ... that way if things go wrong you’re close by and it just makes things easier.

6
00:02:37,997 --> 00:02:52,069
<v Woman> Let me write this down ... Right. Yes. The plumber who fixed things yesterday was from quite far away but I chose him because his advert said he did emergency repairs.

7
00:02:52,069 --> 00:03:05,814
<v Man> Well, fair enough ... you needed something in a hurry. But another piece of advice I’d give is try to avoid calling anybody on weekends. That’ll really bump up the prices. Leave it till Monday, if you can.

8
00:03:05,814 --> 00:03:16,146
<v Woman> Well, yes ... I think I can do that because the temporary fix should hold. And obviously I’ll need the ceiling plastered and eventually re-decorated.

9
00:03:16,146 --> 00:03:17,159
<v Man> Yes, sure.

10
00:03:17,159 --> 00:03:21,408
<v Woman> So who would you recommend? Is there a directory?

11
00:03:21,408 --> 00:03:29,358
<v Man> Well, there’s quite a good website covering this sort of work. It’s www.plasdeco.com.

12
00:03:29,358 --> 00:03:30,921
<v Woman> Is that with a K?

13
00:03:30,921 --> 00:03:37,792
<v Man> A C, P-L-A-S-D-E-C-O dot com.

14
00:03:37,792 --> 00:03:42,359
<v Woman> Got it. Well I’ll try and have a look at that.

15
00:03:42,359 --> 00:03:45,606
<v Man> Yes, it gives price and quality comparisons.

16
00:03:45,606 --> 00:03:55,374
<v Woman> Oh, that’ll be useful, but I find personal recommendations really helpful as well ... you know, you can find out whether you can rely on the company.

17
00:03:55,374 --> 00:03:59,402
<v Man> Well, I know a couple of reasonable plumbers and also some plasterers.

18
00:03:59,402 --> 00:04:00,455
<v Woman> Great.

19
00:04:33,469 --> 00:04:46,058
<v Man> There’s a company called Peake’s Plumbing ... now they’re a father and son team. They’re really friendly and they tell you information you need in a clear way ... you know, so they really understand what the problem is.

20
00:04:46,058 --> 00:04:50,419
<v Woman> Right, well that’s good to know. Are they reliable?

21
00:04:50,419 --> 00:04:57,923
<v Man> Well, that’s a down side - every single time I’ve used them they arrive late. And friends have said the same thing.

22
00:04:57,923 --> 00:05:00,648
<v Woman> But is the work good quality?

23
00:05:00,648 --> 00:05:06,941
<v Man> Absolutely ... Another one is John Damerol Plumbing Services - he’s very good.

24
00:05:06,941 --> 00:05:09,191
<v Woman> How do you spell the surname?

25
00:05:09,191 --> 00:05:12,646
<v Man> D-A-M-E-R-O-L.

26
00:05:12,646 --> 00:05:17,725
<v Woman> Right ... got that. And does he  do high quality work?

27
00:05:17,725 --> 00:05:26,527
<v Man> Well, it’s fine, you know, but I wouldn’t say that was his main point. Basically he comes out cheaper ... you know ... than other people.

28
00:05:26,527 --> 00:05:30,744
<v Woman> I sense there’s a ‘but’ ... is he unreliable?

29
00:05:30,744 --> 00:05:42,741
<v Man> Oh ... he comes when he says he’s coming BUT he’s not very courteous and he has the tendency to be messy ... you know so you have quite a bit of clearing up to do.

30
00:05:42,964 --> 00:05:44,628
<v Woman> Hmmm ... OK.

31
00:05:44,628 --> 00:05:48,674
<v Man> So it’s up to you ... they’re both good workers and they won’t cheat you.

32
00:05:48,674 --> 00:05:52,886
<v Woman> Right. And you said you knew some plasterers?

33
00:05:52,886 --> 00:06:03,116
<v Man> Yes a company called Simonson Plasterers did our living room last year ... we chose them because we wanted some fancy work on the ceiling - around the lights.

34
00:06:03,116 --> 00:06:06,657
<v Woman> So they can do a variety of designs?

35
00:06:06,657 --> 00:06:11,561
<v Man> You’ve got it. But it comes at a premium because they are more expensive ... you know ...

36
00:06:11,561 --> 00:06:12,942
<v Woman> ... than the others ...

37
00:06:12,942 --> 00:06:22,968
<v Man> Yes ... Or you could go for a one-man firm called H.L. Plastering ... Harry Lester - he’s fine - very reliable, if all you want is a simple job ...

38
00:06:22,968 --> 00:06:29,051
<v Woman> Do either of them do painting for you if you want ... ? After the plastering’s dried out of course.

39
00:06:29,051 --> 00:06:37,726
<v Man> That’s what I was going to say. But I should explain that Harry’s quite old now and so he avoids doing jobs which involve tall ladders ... you know.

40
00:06:37,726 --> 00:06:43,377
<v Woman> But my kitchen isn’t too bad for that ... I’d have to ask him if he’s prepared to do it.

41
00:06:43,377 --> 00:06:44,852
<v Man> Yeah sure.

42
00:06:44,852 --> 00:06:47,912
<v Woman> So I’ll start by looking at the website.

43
00:06:47,912 --> 00:06:51,634
<v Man> All those companies are on there ... with their phone numbers etc ...

44
00:06:51,634 --> 00:06:54,701
<v Woman> Thanks ever so much ...